1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,518
When DNA copies itself, what happens to the old strands?

2
00:00:04,518 --> 00:00:06,367
There were three ideas.

3
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:11,445
Conservative: the old molecule stays whole and a brand new one is made.

4
00:00:11,445 --> 00:00:17,304
Semi conservative: the strands separate, and each daughter keeps one old strand.

5
00:00:17,304 --> 00:00:21,393
Dispersive: old and new pieces scattered through both.

